Here's the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic catalog** audit of `OrderProcessorTests.cs`.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 4           | 4              |
| Medium   | 5           | 4              |
| Low      | 1           | —  (class-level)|
| **Total**| **10**      | **7 of 8**     |

Only **one** test method (`ValidateOrder_NullOrder_ThrowsArgumentNullException`) is smell-free.

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH

#### 1. Conditional Test Logic
**File:** `OrderProcessorTests.cs` · **Method:** `ProcessOrder_SetsCorrectStatus` (line 24)

```csharp
if (result.TotalAmount > 100)
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
else
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
```

One branch is **never exercised** — the test always passes yet only validates half the logic.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_SmallOrder_SetsStandardStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-CHEAP", 1) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_LargeOrder_SetsPremiumStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-EXPENSIVE", 5) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden gap — one status path is never verified.

---

#### 2. Assertion-Free Test (a.k.a. Unknown Test)
**File:** `OrderProcessorTests.cs` · **Method:** `ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError` (line 43)

```csharp
processor.ProcessOrder(order);
// no assertion at all
```

The test passes as long as no exception is thrown, but it verifies **nothing** about the result.

**Fix — assert observable outcomes:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    var result = processor.ProcessOrder(order);

    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage increases but defects go undetected.

---

#### 3. Sleepy Test
**File:** `OrderProcessorTests.cs` · **Method:** `ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent` (line 91)

```csharp
processor.ProcessOrderAsync(order);
Thread.Sleep(2000);
Assert.IsTrue(_email.WasNotificationSent(order.Id));
```

A 2-second wall-clock sleep makes the suite slow and non-deterministic; the delay may be too short in CI.

**Fix — `await` the async work or use a polling helper:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent()
